## Patch 2 — `src/index.css` (additive, appended)

Append this block at the end of the file. It uses `:where()` (zero specificity) so it never overrides Tailwind utilities emitted by the CVA, and it does not set `transform` or `box-shadow` globally, so framer-motion parents are untouched.

```
------- SEARCH
=======
/* ============================================================
   Luxury 3D Button System — global support layer.
   Low-specificity via :where() so per-instance Tailwind utilities
   from buttonVariants always win. No transform/box-shadow set here,
   to avoid conflicts with framer-motion and page layouts.
   ============================================================ */
@layer base {
  :where(button:not(:disabled)),
  :where([role="button"]:not([aria-disabled="true"])) {
    -webkit-tap-highlight-color: transparent;
  }
}

/* Reduced-motion guarantee at the document level as a safety net,
   in case a utility class is purged in a given build. */
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  :where(.transform-gpu) {
    transition: none !important;
    transform: none !important;
  }
}
