## Root-Cause & Impact Analysis

This is not a bug fix — it is a centralized visual upgrade. The right lever is exactly the one the task identifies: `buttonVariants` in `src/components/ui/button.jsx`. Because the component's public contract (`variant`, `size`, `asChild`, `className`, `disabled`, ref forwarding) stays identical, every consumer inherits the new look with zero call-site changes. That is the clean part of the surface.

Blast radius (from the caller list): `buttonVariants` is consumed two ways — directly via `<Button>` (MFASetup, AuditLog, ChangePassword) and indirectly via `cn(buttonVariants({...}))` inside other primitives (`alert-dialog`, `calendar`, `carousel`, `pagination`, `sidebar`). Changing the variant/size class strings therefore propagates into those primitives too. This is intended (centralization), but it means the `size` tokens (especially `icon`, `h-9 w-9`) must stay stable so `pagination`/`carousel` icon buttons keep their geometry. I am leaving all four size presets untouched for this reason.

Regression risks I am actively mitigating:

1. `transition-colors` → animating everything. Switching to `transition-all` would animate layout-adjacent properties and can fight framer-motion on animated pages. I scope the transition to `transform, box-shadow, background-color, border-color` only.
2. Hover elevation uses `translate-y`, a transform — it does not reflow flex/grid layouts, so Monthly Calendar / Room Board / OTA Channels grids won't shift.
3. Test coupling. The existing tests assert old token classes (`bg-destructive`, `bg-secondary`, `hover:bg-accent`, `text-primary`). A redesign necessarily invalidates those specific assertions; the task explicitly authorizes updating the test file, so I update those assertions and add coverage for the new depth/motion classes. All behavioral tests (disabled, click suppression, ref, asChild, custom className) are preserved unchanged.
4. Focus ring: `ring-offset` needs an explicit offset color or it defaults to white against the dark canvas. I set `ring-offset` to `--s-canvas`.
5. Global `button {}` element rules in `index.css` (element selector, specificity 0,0,1) lose to Tailwind utility classes (0,1,0), so the component classes win — but I add a guarded, additive block rather than editing rules I cannot see.

