## Patch 3 — `src/index.css` (additive — review before applying)

I could not see the current file, so this is an append-only block rather than a SEARCH/REPLACE against unknown content. Add it after your existing `@layer base`. It ensures native/framer-motion buttons don't clash with the component's transform-based elevation and honors reduced-motion globally.

```css
### FILE: src/index.css (append)

@layer utilities {
  /* Luxury 3D button support: keep transforms on their own compositor layer
     so hover lift / active press stay smooth alongside framer-motion. */
  .btn-3d-surface {
    transform: translateZ(0);
    backface-visibility: hidden;
  }
}

@layer base {
  /* The shared <Button> owns its own transitions via utility classes.
     Prevent any global `button { transition: ... }` rule from double-animating
     or overriding the scoped transition. Utilities (0,1,0) already beat this
     element selector (0,0,1); this is a defensive reset only. */
  button {
    -webkit-tap-highlight-color: transparent;
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    button {
      transition: none !important;
    }
  }
}
```

